  "id": "COMPOUND:19331 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Spiculoic acid A is implicated in the targeting of Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Spiculoic acid A directly interacts with the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is a target of a complex, highly structured molecule with multiple stereoisomers. This molecule, which is a derivative of a long-chain hydrocarbon, is known to be a target of SNU-387, a compound that in turn targets Replicase polyprotein 1ab. Additionally, SNU-387 is also a target of Phomalide, which also leads to the same downstream effect on Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these pathways indicates that Spiculoic acid A may act through a shared mechanism involving the activation of a target that ultimately leads to the inhibition of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The evidence supports a potential role for Spiculoic acid A in modulating the activity of Replicase polyprotein 1ab via a chain of targets, highlighting a possible dependency on the complex molecular structure of the intermediates involved.",
